.wt/

# EVIDENCE RECORDS ARE NOT COMMITTED, in either shape, and the reason is what an
# attestation is for. A record made on a developer machine attests to whatever
# tools happened to be installed there; it is a convenience for the person who
# ran it, not something a third party can rely on. The durable record is the one
# CI writes on a clean tree and uploads as an artifact, whose provenance is the
# run that produced it.
#
# Committing them would also lag by one: the record for commit N can only exist
# after N does, so it would always land in N+1 and describe its parent.
#
# See .prod/evidence/README.md.
.prod/evidence/*.json
